  "result": "Perfect! All 103 tests pass. Here's a summary of the tier discount implementation:\n\n## Customer Tier Discounts \u2705\n\nI've successfully implemented automatic tier discounts for customers. Here's what was added:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. src/customers.js**\n- Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant with tier-specific discount percentages:\n  - `gold: 5%`\n  - `silver: 2.5%`\n  - `standard: 0%`\n\n**2. src/invoices.js**\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to automatically apply tier discounts:\n  - When a line has no explicit `discountPercent`, the customer's tier discount is applied\n  - Explicit `discountPercent` (even 0) always overrides tier discount\n  - Tier discount is stored as `discountPercent` on the line\n\n**3. test/invoices.test.js**\n- Added 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Each tier applies correct default discount (gold 5%, silver 2.5%, standard 0%)\n  - Explicit `discountPercent` overrides tier discount\n  - Explicit 0% discount overrides tier discount (important distinction)\n  - Multiple lines with mixed explicit and tier discounts\n  - `invoiceTotals` calculates correctly with tier discounts\n  - Tier discounts persist through `issueInvoice`\n  - `addLine` does NOT apply tier discounts (only for `createInvoice`)\n- Fixed 1 existing test to account for new tier discount behavior\n\n### Key Features:\n- \u2705 Tier discounts applied automatically when creating invoices\n- \u2705 Explicit `discountPercent` (including 0) always wins\n- \u2705 Centralized `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant for easy maintenance\n- \u2705 All 103 tests passing (90 original + 13 new)",
